   "text": "The vase is modeled, but the plan check did not fully pass, so I have not called it done.\n\nThe outer body is an 80 mm across-corners hexagon, 160 mm tall, twisting 60 degrees from bottom to top, with an open top and a 3 mm solid floor. The check failed on feature count (want 3, got 2) because the floor is formed by where the cavity starts rather than as its own step. The minimum wall measures **1.68 mm** against the 2 mm you asked for, probably at the corners where the smooth loft diverges from the offset inner cavity.\n\nHow do you want to go on?\n- Keep the geometry as it is and accept the feature-count mismatch, or split the cavity into two steps so the count matches.\n- Tighten the inner cavity so the wall holds 2 mm at the corners.\n\nOnce you pick, I'll rebuild, re-check, and then slice it for the P1S in PLA with the 0.4 mm nozzle if you want it printed."
